{"overview":{"Symbol":"ARXS","Name":"Arxis, Inc.","Description":"Arxis, Inc. designs and manufactures electronic and mechanical components for mission critical applications in the United States. The company operates through two segments: Electronic Components and Mechanical Components. Its Electronic Components segment provides engineered electronic components and interconnect solutions, including connectors, cable assemblies, microelectronic packaging, radio frequency (RF) and microwave products, power products, sensors, capacitors. and resistors. The Mechanical Components segment offers precision and self-lubricating bearings, seals, springs, gaskets and ducting, and radar absorbing materials. It serves defense and space systems, commercial aerospace platforms, medical technology, semiconductor testing, analytical devices, industrial automation, and other specialized industrial sectors. The company was founded in 2019 and is based in Bloomfield, Connecticut.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NasdaqGS","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Industrials","Industry":"Aerospace & Defense","Address":"1332 Blue Hills Avenue, Bloomfield, CT, 06002, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"16712933376","EBITDA":"533535008","PERatio":"2036.5","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"7.758","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"0.02","RevenuePerShareTTM":"4.069","ProfitMargin":"0.06206","OperatingMarginTTM":"0.24239999","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"","RevenueTTM":"1669799040","GrossProfitTTM":"827393024","DilutedEPSTTM":"0.02","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"0.207","AnalystTargetPrice":"52.3","TrailingPE":"2036.5","ForwardPE":"43.99961","PriceToSalesRatioTTM":"10.008949","PriceToBookRatio":"5.2500644","EVToRevenue":"11.328","EVToEBITDA":"35.453","Beta":"","52WeekHigh":"48.68","52WeekLow":"33.15","50DayMovingAverage":"37.596153","200DayMovingAverage":"37.596153","SharesOutstanding":"69657950","Divi